{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li0 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri10080 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li-760 
{\b1 \cf18 \f2 \ri10080 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li-760 
{\b1 \cf18 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa100 \sb0 
23-004
\par 
}
}
}
{\b0 \cf23 \f2 \i0 \fs20 
}
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat42 
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
Documentary
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat2 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 
}
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat42 
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
credits
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat2 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 benefit from an unparalleled measure of harmonisation of commercial law through the worldwide adoption by banks of a set of rules promulgated by the International Chamber of Commerce (
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
ICC
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
) and known as the 
}
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat42 
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
Uniform
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat2 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 
}
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat42 
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
Customs
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat2 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 and 
}
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat42 
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
Practice
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat2 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 for 
}
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat42 
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
Documentary
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat2 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 
}
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat42 
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
Credits
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat2 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 (UCP). The origin of this uniquely successful instrument lies in the surge of international trade after the end of the First World War, the inconvenience caused by the lack of a standard approach to a widely used instrument for financing that trade, and the response of the banking sector. The critical initiative was the adoption by the New York Bankers\u8217\'3f Commercial Credit Conference of 1920 of the Regulations Affecting Export Commercial 
}
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat42 
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
Credits
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat2 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
, which also incorporated the recently promulgated American Foreign Trade Definitions. Revised in 1926, these Regulations inspired the adoption of domestic rules governing 
}
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat42 
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
documentary
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat2 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 
}
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat42 
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
credits
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat2 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 by banks in several countries and the suggestion that the 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
ICC
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 should seek to develop an instrument that would gain international acceptance.
\par 
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li0 
{\b0 \cf23 \f2 \i0 \fs20 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
After draft instruments of 1927 and 1929, the first 
}
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat42 
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
revision
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat2 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 of the UCP was formally adopted by the Seventh Congress of the 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
ICC
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
, held in Vienna in 1933. It was adopted by the banks in a number of European countries and, from 1938, also by a significant number of banks in the US, albeit only for export 
}
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat42 
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
credits
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat2 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 and subject to the American Foreign Trade Definitions. As might be expected, there were no developments of any significance during the Second World War. However, in 1949 the 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
ICC
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 commenced work on a revised version of the UCP, leading to adoption of the 1951 
}
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat42 
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
Revision
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat2 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 at the 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
ICC
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
\u8217\'3fs 13th Congress, held in Lisbon. It was adhered to by banks in a substantial number of countries in Asia, Africa, Europe and the US. In the US, the qualifications attached to adoption of the 1933 
}
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat42 
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
Revision
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat2 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 were initially maintained with respect to the 1951 
}
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat42 
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
Revision
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat2 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 but were dropped in 1956. Henceforth, the UCP was accepted by US banks as applicable to both export and import 
}
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat42 
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
credits
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat2 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb200 
, and the American Foreign Trade Definitions, which had been revised in 1941, were no longer incorporated\u8212\'3fmore generally, they had been superseded by Incoterms.
\par 
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li0 
{\b0 \cf23 \f2 \i0 \fs20 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
The 1951 
}
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat42 
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
Revision
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat2 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 was, however, rejected, partly for political reasons, by banks in the UK and, consequently, in most Commonwealth countries. Nevertheless, the commercial need for a truly international instrument could not be denied, and the UK and Commonwealth banks participated in the preparation of, and duly adopted, the 1962 
}
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat42 
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
Revision
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat2 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 of the UCP. This 
}
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat42 
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
Revision
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat2 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
, therefore, saw the UCP achieve the status of a truly worldwide instrument regulating 
}
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat42 
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
documentary
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat2 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 
}
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat42 
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
credits
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat2 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 in all parts of the globe, albeit technically on an optional basis.
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs16 
