{\b0 \cf23 \f2 \i0 \fs20 
}
{\b0 \cf40 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa160 \sb320 
Status and applicability of the UCP
\par 
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li0 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri10080 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li-760 
{\b1 \cf18 \f2 \ri10080 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li-760 
{\b1 \cf18 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa100 \sb0 
23-006
\par 
}
}
}
{\b0 \cf23 \f2 \i0 \fs20 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
The UCP does not have force of law in the UK.
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs16 
{\*\bkmkstart co_fnRef_08729e5a-6a69-436d-8235-88b1a73}{\*\bkmkend co_fnRef_08729e5a-6a69-436d-8235-88b1a73}
{\field {\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#co_footnote_08729e5a-6a69-436d-8235-88b1" }{\fldrslt 
{\super \b0 \cf23 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs15 \sa0 \sb0 
13
}}}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 Its status is that of a set of standard contractual terms with its application dependent on incorporation into the credit and subject to any mandatory rules of the applicable national law.
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs16 
{\*\bkmkstart co_fnRef_33a48885-3f56-4190-83f7-5663a06}{\*\bkmkend co_fnRef_33a48885-3f56-4190-83f7-5663a06}
{\field {\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#co_footnote_33a48885-3f56-4190-83f7-5663" }{\fldrslt 
{\super \b0 \cf23 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs15 \sa0 \sb0 
14
}}}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 UCP 600 Art.1 accordingly provides, consistently with previous 
}
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat42 
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
revisions
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat2 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 of the UCP, that the rules of the UCP \u8220\'3fapply to any 
}
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat42 
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
documentary
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat2 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 credit \u8230\'3f when the text of the credit expressly indicates that it is subject to [its] rules\u8221\'3f.
\par 
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li0 
{\b0 \cf23 \f2 \i0 \fs20 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
Nevertheless, whether terms are incorporated into a contract depends on the intention of the parties to that contract rather than the target provisions.
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs16 
{\*\bkmkstart co_fnRef_af927c5a-c21b-4b2f-a8d5-d7e7de0}{\*\bkmkend co_fnRef_af927c5a-c21b-4b2f-a8d5-d7e7de0}
{\field {\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#co_footnote_af927c5a-c21b-4b2f-a8d5-d7e7" }{\fldrslt 
{\super \b0 \cf23 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs15 \sa0 \sb0 
15
}}}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 Where the UCP has been expressly incorporated into a series of 
}
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat42 
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
credits
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat2 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 between a bank and a seller, and a credit is subsequently issued that does not mention the UCP, it may be inferred that it was intended to incorporate the UCP, and Art.1 will not preclude a court from giving effect to that intention.
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs16 
{\*\bkmkstart co_fnRef_2d80fe3f-99ec-4c9b-92ef-a1bbd3a}{\*\bkmkend co_fnRef_2d80fe3f-99ec-4c9b-92ef-a1bbd3a}
{\field {\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#co_footnote_2d80fe3f-99ec-4c9b-92ef-a1bb" }{\fldrslt 
{\super \b0 \cf23 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs15 \sa0 \sb0 
16
}}}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 At one time, moreover, the SWIFT messages by which the terms of 
}
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat42 
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
credits
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat2 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 are generally communicated between banks used not to provide for express incorporation of the UCP by those terms, but the SWIFT user handbook provided that all 
}
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat42 
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
credits
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat2 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 communicated via SWIFT were subject to the UCP. Notwithstanding the failure to conform to the incorporation requirement of the UCP, the ICC Banking Commission recognised that SWIFT users would be bound by the terms of the handbook but stated that an express incorporation clause should be included in any communication between a bank in receipt of a SWIFT message and the beneficiary.
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs16 
{\*\bkmkstart co_fnRef_50e0eec4-956d-4464-a1e7-059d538}{\*\bkmkend co_fnRef_50e0eec4-956d-4464-a1e7-059d538}
{\field {\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#co_footnote_50e0eec4-956d-4464-a1e7-059d" }{\fldrslt 
{\super \b0 \cf23 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs15 \sa0 \sb0 
17
}}}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb200 
 SWIFT messages have since been changed to include express incorporation of the UCP in line with Art.1.
\par 
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li0 
{\b0 \cf23 \f2 \i0 \fs20 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
Suppose, nevertheless, that a credit were issued with no clause incorporating the UCP and in the absence of any evidence relating to previous transactions or showing that the failure to incorporate the UCP was occasioned by a technical error. In this unlikely eventuality, it is suggested that English law would still consider the UCP the best evidence of the terms the parties must have intended. It has been used extensively by banks in the UK and elsewhere since 1962, and knowledge of its existence and of its general implications can be attributed also to most firms active in the import and export of goods. 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
Indeed, the UCP is better known and more widely used than the 
}
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat42 
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
Uniform
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat2 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 Rules for Collections, which have been held to apply even in transactions in which they are not expressly incorporated in the relevant documentation.
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs16 
{\*\bkmkstart co_fnRef_28fe235f-461e-4143-8042-a1cf884}{\*\bkmkend co_fnRef_28fe235f-461e-4143-8042-a1cf884}
{\field {\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#co_footnote_28fe235f-461e-4143-8042-a1cf" }{\fldrslt 
{\super \b0 \cf23 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs15 \sa0 \sb0 
18
}}}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb200 
 Moreover, the alternative, unless the contract is void for uncertainty, is to attribute to the parties the highly implausible intention that the credit be governed by a common law essentially moribund since the adoption of the UCP.
\par 
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
\u160\'3f
\par 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li0 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 
}
{\b0 \cf40 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \ql \fs20 \li0 
{\b0 \cf23 \f2 \i0 \fs20 
}
{\b0 \cf23 \f2 \i0 \fs20 
}
{\b0 \cf40 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa160 \sb320 
Interpretation in law
\par 
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li0 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri10080 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li-760 
{\b1 \cf18 \f2 \ri10080 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li-760 
{\b1 \cf18 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa100 \sb0 
23-007
\par 
}
}
}
{\b0 \cf23 \f2 \i0 \fs20 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
Consistent with their contractual status, the provisions of the UCP fall to be construed in accordance with the normal approach to commercial contracts.
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs16 
{\*\bkmkstart co_fnRef_1d206a42-d67e-4431-aae5-d953239}{\*\bkmkend co_fnRef_1d206a42-d67e-4431-aae5-d953239}
