35
}}}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 a credit incorporating the 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb200 
UCP provided 10 per cent of the credit was payable:
\par 
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri400 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li700 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri400 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li700 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri400 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li700 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri400 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li700 
{\b0 \cf23 \f2 \i0 \fs20 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb200 
\u8220\'3f\u8230\'3f within sixty days from date of completion of discharging and after assurance that consignment strictly complying for specifications mentioned in credit terms and after we advise you our principal\u8217\'3fs instructions.\u8221\'3f
\par 
}
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa200 \sb0 
\u160\'3f
\par 
}
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li0 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
This \u8220\'3fobscure\u8221\'3f provision was held to mean that the remaining 10 per cent became payable under the credit 60 days after the date of discharge if the applicant had by then failed to object to the quality of the goods, or earlier if the applicant so instructed. Such a condition, it was conceded, \u8220\'3foffends against \u8230\'3f the first rule of letters of credit, namely that the parties are dealing in documents, not facts\u8221\'3f,
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs16 
{\*\bkmkstart co_fnRef_02fcb0ea-5c17-4dc6-a2b8-3984acf}{\*\bkmkend co_fnRef_02fcb0ea-5c17-4dc6-a2b8-3984acf}
{\field {\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#co_footnote_02fcb0ea-5c17-4dc6-a2b8-3984" }{\fldrslt 
{\super \b0 \cf23 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs15 \sa0 \sb0 
36
}}}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 and is also open to the 
}
{\field {\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://uk.westlaw.com/Link/Document/FullText?findType=Y&serNum=1986026480&pubNum=4891&originatingDoc=I8CC6FA006E3211E782BDB54604FBEE92&refType=UC&originationContext=document&vr=3.0&rs=PLUK1.0&transitionType=CommentaryUKLink&contextData=(sc.Search)" }{\fldrslt 
{\b0 \cf23 \f2 \i1 \fs20 
{\b0 \cf23 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i1 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
Forestal Mimosa
}
}}}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 criticism that a credit is designed not be controlled by the applicant. However, the alternative interpretation was that the remaining 10 per cent became payable only once the buyer expressly approved payment. This was even further removed from the commercial understanding of a 
}
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat42 
{\b1 \cf24 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
documentary
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 \chcbpat2 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 credit and was duly rejected; the suggestion that a beneficiary that had presented complying documents might have to wait indefinitely for payment because of entirely capricious behaviour by the applicant was so bizarre as to be an untenable interpretation.
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs16 
{\*\bkmkstart co_fnRef_340bde4b-8678-429d-a3db-4a953a3}{\*\bkmkend co_fnRef_340bde4b-8678-429d-a3db-4a953a3}
